{
  "id": "discourse_argument",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "depends_on": [
    "dialogue_intertext",
    "event_reasoning"
  ],
  "description": "Discourse coherence (RST clause->clause relations = within-text dialogue relations, connective-typed) and argument (Toulmin claim/evidence/warrant; sound iff the warrant licenses a firing implication; named fallacies for circular/ad-hominem/affirming-the-consequent). Both compose existing machinery: the relation classifier + the inference engine + suspect-witness belief.",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "discourse_argument",
    "description": "RST coherence + argument validity"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "local_id": 1,
      "type": "Concept",
      "attrs": {
        "name": "discourse_coherence",
        "description": "RST: relations BETWEEN adjacent clauses in one text \u2014 the DIALOGUE-relation faculty with the speaker held constant. The same relation classifier types clause->clause edges as cause/contrast/concession/elaboration/sequence from connectives (because/but/although/for-example/then) + referent-overlap (shared roles->elaboration). The monologue sibling of conversational coherence; output = a nucleus/satellite tree over clauses."
      }
    },
    {
      "local_id": 2,
      "type": "Concept",
      "attrs": {
        "name": "argument",
        "description": "A coherence relation with a TRUTH OBLIGATION, one level above RST. A Toulmin Frame (claim/evidence/warrant \u2014 three role-slots, same Frame machinery as semantic roles); VALIDITY = the warrant licenses an Implication that actually fires under the inference engine; FALLACY = the relation asserts support but no valid Implication connects evidence to claim, scored by the believe/refute (suspect-witness) rule. Argument = RST-relation + entailment-check + belief-scoring."
      }
    },
    {
      "local_id": 3,
      "type": "Principle",
      "attrs": {
        "name": "rst_is_dialogue_within",
        "head": "discourse/argument",
        "body": "discourse coherence is the dialogue relation with one speaker; reuse the relation classifier, just widen the domain to clause->clause inside a paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "local_id": 4,
      "type": "Principle",
      "attrs": {
        "name": "argument_composes",
        "head": "discourse/argument",
        "body": "argument adds nothing new: Toulmin frame + the warrant-licenses-an-implication entailment check + suspect-witness belief-scoring; circular = warrant==claim, ad hominem = evidence about the person not the proposition, affirming-the-consequent = wrong implication direction"
      }
    }
  ],
